{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["C6", "R10"],
      "pins": ["C6.1", "C6.2"],
      "nets": ["/PWM1", "/PWM1_C2"],
      "observed": "C6 is a 100u capacitor connected between /PWM1 and /PWM1_C2 (J1/J2 pin 21). The netlist contains no R10 component, although the spec calls for R9–R12 to be 0Ω jumpers selecting the PWM source pins.",
      "expected": "R10 should be a 0Ω jumper (or resistor) between /PWM1 and /PWM1_C2, so that shorting it selects M5Stack bus pin 21 as the PWM1 source for Core2/CoreS3. A capacitor in this position is not a jumper and cannot pass the PWM signal.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C6\") (value \"100u\") (footprint \"Capacitor_SMD:C_1206_3216Metric_Pad1.33x1.80mm_HandSolder\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"22\") (name \"/PWM1\") ... (node (ref \"C6\") (pin \"1\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"24\") (name \"/PWM1_C2\") ... (node (ref \"C6\") (pin \"2\") ...)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2 — schematic note: \"Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others\""
        }
      ],
      "impact": "For Core2/CoreS3, PWM1 cannot be connected to bus pin 21; instead the 100u capacitor AC-couples the PWM1 line to pin 21, heavily loading and distorting the PWM signal, so the channel-1 servo will not be driven correctly. If R9 is also populated, the capacitor places a large AC load between two GPIO pins.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an anomaly: C6 is a 100u capacitor placed in the R10 0Ω jumper position between /PWM1 and /PWM1_C2, and R10 is missing. This prevents proper PWM1 source selection for Core2/CoreS3 and would distort the PWM1 signal."
}

